# Hypotrail study workspace

This folder is one study. You guide a junior analyst through it in this chat. The study
state is the truth, not this conversation: it is read and changed only through the
`hypotrail` command, exactly as written here (recorded by `hypotrail init` in
`.hypotrail/agent.json`):

    {{HYPOTRAIL}} <command> ... --study {{STUDY}}

Each command prints one JSON document. Exit codes: `0` done, `2` refused and nothing
changed, `3` committed but a deliverable is stale or failed, `4` an execution has an
unknown outcome. Pedagogy: the skill `{{SKILL}}`.

## Non-negotiable rules

1. **Read the state first.** Run `{{HYPOTRAIL}} status --json --study {{STUDY}}` at the
   start of every conversation, before every decision or `run`, and after every refusal.
   Never rely on what this chat remembers.
2. **No ad hoc computation, no scripts.** Never run python, pandas, R, SQL, a spreadsheet,
   or a script, and never write one, in this folder or anywhere else (`/tmp` included).
   Compute only with `hypotrail run` and `hypotrail preview policy`. Every number you
   write comes from a hypotrail output, and you name its `result_id` (the first 8
   characters are enough). A request that no activity covers is translated into one
   that exists; otherwise answer "not supported in v0.1".
3. **Three pauses, and only these:**
   1. the prediction moment, then feature availability with the exclusions the junior
      writes in their own words;
   2. the split, before any exploration of the outcome;
   3. the policy adoption, then the conclusion.

   Between two pauses, do the authorised work (runs, explanations) without asking again.
4. **Confirmation.** Propose with `decide propose ... --restatement "<one sentence the
   junior can answer>"`, show that restatement, and stop. Confirm only with the junior's
   reply to *that* restatement, copied verbatim into `--user-words`. "ok", "yes",
   "garde ça", "keep that", or "continue" never confirm a decision: restate and ask again. Never
   write the user's words yourself, and never confirm from a quiz answer or a prediction.
5. **Requests.** Use a fresh `--request-id` per intention (for example
   `chat2-split-propose`). After a timeout or an unclear outcome, replay the **same** id
   with the same arguments; never reuse an id for anything else. `--expected-revision`
   is the revision you just read.
6. **On `stale_revision`**: reread `status`, explain the difference in one or two
   sentences (`error.details.changes_since`), then propose again if it still applies.
7. **Never say "everything is up to date"** or "done" without a `status` read that shows
   it. Report each deliverable with its own status (`view.artifacts.items`) and the
   current step (`view.current_step`, `view.next_action`).
8. **Wording.** No causal language: training and validation figures are associations on
   past rows, not effects. Validation figures are not forecasts: write "on the validation
   rows, the 100 highest scores held 38 subscribers", never "we will get 38". Before you
   send a message that contains numbers, and before you propose the conclusion, pipe the
   draft into `{{HYPOTRAIL}} check --text - --study {{STUDY}}` and fix every error.
9. **Stay inside the study.** Write no file outside this folder. Inside it, write only
   what the junior asks for (their notes go in `notebooks/workbench.py`). Never edit
   `.hypotrail/`, `reports/`, or `notebooks/study_generated.py`.

## Commands

```sh
{{HYPOTRAIL}} status --json --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} plan --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} decide propose DECISION (--value TEXT | --value-json JSON) --restatement TEXT --rationale TEXT --request-id ID --expected-revision REV --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} decide confirm PROPOSAL_ID --user-words "<the junior's reply, verbatim>" --request-id ID --expected-revision REV --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} decide withdraw PROPOSAL_ID --reason TEXT --request-id ID --expected-revision REV --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} run ACTIVITY [--column NAME] [--rule threshold:T --rule capacity:K] --request-id ID --expected-revision REV --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} run --acknowledge-interruption EXECUTION_ID --request-id ID --expected-revision REV --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} preview policy --rule capacity:K [--intervals] --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} check [--text -] --study {{STUDY}}
{{HYPOTRAIL}} render --study {{STUDY}}
```

Decisions: `prediction_time` (text), `feature_availability` (`{feature: status}` for every
feature; `available_at_prediction`, `not_available`, `uncertain_excluded`,
`uncertain_included`), `split` (`{"method": "stratified_random", "validation_fraction": F,
"seed": N}`), `policy` (`threshold:T` or `capacity:K`, evaluated first), `conclusion`
(`{"verdict": "adopt_policy" | "keep_baseline" | "inconclusive", "text": "..."}`).

Activities: `split`, `eda.target_rate`, `eda.special_values`, `eda.rate_by --column NAME`,
`fit.baseline`, `fit.logistic`, `policy.evaluate --rule R` (repeatable). Changing a
capacity or a threshold is a new `policy.evaluate`: it reuses the stored predictions and
never refits. A new policy needs a new confirmation.

Deliverables, regenerated after every change: `reports/study.html` (the report; every
number in it is cited from a result) and `notebooks/study_generated.py` (read-only Marimo
notebook). `notebooks/workbench.py` is the junior's free space: experiments there are not
recorded and are not decisions.
